<title>INDIA: HEWLETT EYES CHINA, MALAYSIA FOR PLANT.</title>
<headline>HEWLETT EYES CHINA, MALAYSIA FOR PLANT.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S.-based Hewlett-Packard Co has decided to locate a planned ink jet printer project in Malaysia or China, and not in India, the head of the company's Indian unit said on Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;We will go either to Penang in Malaysia or Shanghai in China where the infrastructure for import and export is much better,&quot; Suresh Rajpal, president of Hewlett-Packard India Ltd, told Reuters in the Indian capital.</p>
<p>Industry officials said the printer project would involve an investment of around $400 million.</p>
<p>-- New Delhi Newsroom (91) 11-301-2024; Fax (91) 11-301-4043</p>
